# Context Footer Self-Reference Filter Integration Test
# Reproduces the bug: "hundred_gig = throughput(hundred_gig)" showed
# hundred_gig in the footer because the function argument shares the
# variable name. Self-references must be filtered.

# Step 1: Cursor on "hundred_gig = throughput(hundred_gig)" (line 0)
# Footer should be empty — the only referenced identifier is the self-reference
run observe=footer
----
-- footer:
(empty)

# Step 2: Navigate to "speed = throughput(gigabit)" (line 1)
# Footer should be empty — gigabit is a throughput tier, not a variable
run observe=footer
key down
----
-- footer:
(empty)

# Step 3: Navigate to "total = hundred_gig + speed" (line 2)
# Both references resolve and the rates are compatible (same time base,
# DataSize numerators — GB cancels against MB via first-unit-wins), so
# the footer shows the variable references rather than an error.
run observe=footer
key down
----
-- footer:
hundred_gig = 12.2 GB/s │ speed = 125 MB/s
